3
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:20,110
Every now and then, I remember that sword fight.

4
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:23,420
That day,

5
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:26,730
I lost my answer, and at the same time I found it.

6
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:30,670
But not a single thing has changed.

7
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:35,290
He's still him, and I'm still me.

8
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:37,430
Only the memories fade away.

9
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:42,770
It's not like either of us believed that anything would change as a result of that fight.

10
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:47,940
Two years have passed

11
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,100
since I faced off with my ideal.

12
00:00:52,410 --> 00:00:53,700
I won't get my answer

13
00:00:54,610 --> 00:00:56,480
for a long, long time yet.

14
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:15,470
{\an4}Epilogue

15
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:15,470
{\an4}Epilogue

16
00:01:11,130 --> 00:01:15,470
{\an4}Epilogue

17
00:01:13,430 --> 00:01:15,590
Thanks for always being so considerate.

18
00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:20,340
But I've told you a million times that I can manage without breakfast.

19
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:23,070
I can't have that.

20
00:01:23,070 --> 00:01:24,830
You're allowing me to live here,

21
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:27,120
so it's the least I can do as your attendant.

22
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:32,200
You're still not a morning person, huh?

23
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,110
That's surprising.

24
00:01:34,450 --> 00:01:37,740
Having at least one little quirk like that

25
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:40,110
gives a girl some charm, right?

26
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:55,510
Schedule-wise,

27
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:58,910
I have a special lecture on cutting in mineralogy today.

28
00:01:58,910 --> 00:01:59,890
How about you?

29
00:01:59,890 --> 00:02:03,090
I think I just have core subjects all morning.

30
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:05,370
Then we're together half the day.

31
00:02:05,370 --> 00:02:07,270
Let's meet at our usual spot this afternoon.

32
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:12,150
Tohsaka...

33
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:15,730
Actually, never mind.

34
00:02:27,550 --> 00:02:28,700
What's the matter?

35
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:30,290
Do you know that person?

36
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:34,050
No, we've just walked by each other a few times.

37
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,550
I was just thinking...

38
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:40,260
This is a bit belated, but it just hit me how strange this is.

39
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:44,650
Why is an outsider like me being allowed to study magic at a place like this?

40
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:46,560
For the last time, you aren't an outsider.

41
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:49,060
I told you Clock Tower's rules, remember?

42
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,830
When you're a noted mage's rightful heir,

43
00:02:51,830 --> 00:02:54,320
you're always at risk of having others try to kill you.

44
00:02:54,930 --> 00:03:01,950
Given that, a mage has the right to be accompanied by a follower or pupil for their protection.

45
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:05,560
You're enrolled here as my follower,

46
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,580
so hold your head up high.

47
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:11,210
I know that. I'm grateful to you, Tohsaka.

48
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:14,950
You ought to be. Getting you in wasn't easy.

49
00:03:14,950 --> 00:03:17,840
Well, it's only a three-year special exemption.

50
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:20,090
But be careful.

51
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:23,320
As a school, this place has rules,

52
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:25,720
but none of the normal social laws.

53
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:28,780
It may only be considered a "minor ritual in the Far East,"

54
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:33,360
but you're a mage who survived the Holy Grail War.

55
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:36,080
Some here won't take kindly to that,

56
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,360
so if you let down your guard...

57
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,610
Your guard is down!

58
00:03:38,610 --> 00:03:40,500
Guess again!

59
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:48,370
Sherou!

60
00:03:48,370 --> 00:03:50,270
Luvia-san?

61
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:52,340
Don't be so impersonal!

62
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:55,380
You're not currently on the clock as her butler, right?

63
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:59,340
"Miss Luvia" is perfectly fine, Sherou!

64
00:04:00,210 --> 00:04:03,570
Don't get so chummy with him!

65
00:04:03,570 --> 00:04:05,840
Oh, Miss Tohsaka...

66
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:10,390
Not only are we classmates, we're also neighbors living in the same apartment building.

67
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:13,670
What's so inappropriate about this?

68
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:15,500
Everything about it is inappropriate!

69
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,020
Relax, Tohsaka.

70
00:04:17,430 --> 00:04:20,880
Let's try to get along with our classmates, okay?

71
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:25,660
Anyway, we only got the third floor of 
that building thanks to Luvia-san, right?

72
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:27,680
Sherou!

73
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:28,620
Hey!

74
00:04:32,370 --> 00:04:33,560
Don't let it go to your head!

75
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:37,040
Oh, dear! O-Oh, oh, oh, oh!

76
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:39,160
Change in plans!

77
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,670
Our next class will be...

78
00:04:45,510 --> 00:04:47,120
Self-defense.

79
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:50,560
The class where one expresses one's vitality 
through physical ability.

80
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:53,180
The Edelfelt family's designated heir,

81
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:55,150
Luviagelita Edelfelt,

82
00:04:55,150 --> 00:04:57,560
will provide you with a much-needed lesson.

83
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:22,510
Excellent!

84
00:05:22,510 --> 00:05:24,530
You might be mistaken for a gorilla! Miss Gorilla!

85
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:26,380
That's right, keep talking!

86
00:05:28,390 --> 00:05:31,010
It hurts! It hurts so bad!

87
00:05:31,990 --> 00:05:34,770
What's the deal with that new-money bitch?

88
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:38,890
I nailed her right in the medulla oblongata, so why wouldn't she go down?!

89
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:44,900
Luvia-san isn't a bad person, so just—

90
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:47,070
Where did you two meet, anyway?!

91
00:05:47,070 --> 00:05:51,830
Well, not long after we moved here, we both got lost...

92
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:57,580
Ow, ow, ow! Ow!

93
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:01,210
Oh, well.

94
00:06:01,210 --> 00:06:03,470
I'll settle things with her eventually.

95
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:08,590
So, what will you do?

96
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:13,090
You got an invitation, right? 
To officially join the Mages' Association?

97
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:15,600
Yeah.

98
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:21,830
A mage's innate talents are evaluated and recorded, 
along with the nature of their soul.

99
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:24,610
They then become a mage affiliated with Clock Tower.

100
00:06:25,370 --> 00:06:26,740
Isn't that a good thing?

101
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:31,990
Your activities would be restricted in some ways 
because you'd basically be indebted to the Association.

102
00:06:32,330 --> 00:06:36,130
But it comes with a lot of perks for a mage,

103
00:06:36,130 --> 00:06:38,000
so most people would jump at it.

104
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:40,750
Yeah.

105
00:06:41,490 --> 00:06:42,560
I guess you're right.

106
00:06:50,930 --> 00:06:55,860
Becoming a Clock Tower member and a genuine mage...

107
00:06:57,430 --> 00:06:58,770
It's the right decision.

108
00:06:59,190 --> 00:07:02,150
But my beliefs lie elsewhere.

109
00:07:16,930 --> 00:07:18,000
Tohsaka?

110
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:24,340
Sorry, I overslept. I'll start breakfast right now.

111
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:25,250
Emiya-kun...

112
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:29,860
Will you go somewhere with me today?

113
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:56,080
What is this place?

114
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,750
Glastonbury.

115
00:07:57,750 --> 00:08:00,160
A certain king's grave.

116
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:05,070
You said you regretted not getting the chance to say a proper goodbye that day.

117
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:09,290
I'll give you two some time alone.

118
00:08:19,410 --> 00:08:22,750
I forgot that you were a king, Saber.

119
00:08:25,490 --> 00:08:26,990
Thank you.

120
00:08:26,990 --> 00:08:30,080
For what it's worth, I've come a long way since then.

121
00:08:35,810 --> 00:08:37,070
This sure is a nice place.

122
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:38,760
Yeah, it is.

123
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:46,210
It feels weird to think that, in a place like this, people once led lives nothing like ours.

124
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:49,450
Like they say, it's a big old world.

125
00:08:49,450 --> 00:08:52,180
It's already been six months since we came to England.

126
00:08:52,180 --> 00:08:54,870
For me, every day is one surprise after another.

127
00:08:54,870 --> 00:08:56,090
How about you?

128
00:08:56,090 --> 00:08:58,410
Same here.

129
00:08:58,410 --> 00:09:01,050
I've learned how insignificant I am.

130
00:09:01,050 --> 00:09:04,240
I became a Master, fought alongside Saber,

131
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:06,600
and survived the Holy Grail War, right?

132
00:09:06,600 --> 00:09:10,030
I thought I could do anything if I put my mind to it.

133
00:09:10,030 --> 00:09:14,190
But by the very next day, that arrogance had faded away.

134
00:09:14,190 --> 00:09:15,790
I'm not surprised.

135
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:18,870
You never change, Shirou.

136
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:21,430
I understand now.

137
00:09:21,430 --> 00:09:25,020
The Holy Grail War was a major event.

138
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:27,160
But now that I've seen a bit more of the world,

139
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:29,380
it's clear that it was only one event of many.

140
00:09:29,380 --> 00:09:32,080
Still, it left a significant mark

141
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:33,790
and sowed the seeds of change.

142
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:37,330
I might not have personally matured,

143
00:09:37,330 --> 00:09:41,980
but I just saw for myself how special that battle was.

144
00:09:43,390 --> 00:09:45,590
I'm the opposite.

145
00:09:45,590 --> 00:09:49,400
I'm starting to believe it wasn't anything special at all.

146
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:54,130
The Holy Grail War, Clock Tower, simple days like this...

147
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:56,380
They'll never fundamentally change.

148
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:59,060
You relied on Saber,

149
00:09:59,060 --> 00:10:03,910
but in her life, Saber herself relied on the people of the past.

150
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:06,380
We're all connected.

151
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:08,400
I think we walk through life 
not only on our own feet,

152
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:12,020
but also by standing on the shoulders 
of those who came before.

153
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:16,790
Clock Tower is steeped in ancient traditions.

154
00:10:16,790 --> 00:10:20,930
So every day, while I'm studying, 
I feel like someone is judging me.

155
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:25,430
Like they're asking what my contribution will be.

156
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:27,280
Oh, I get it.

157
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:30,560
It was that simple, huh?

158
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:48,040
Hey! Wake up, numbskull!

159
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:57,890
Everyone's already left for the assembly!

160
00:10:57,890 --> 00:11:00,300
Are you boycotting it or something?

161
00:11:01,270 --> 00:11:02,050
Hurry!

162
00:11:02,050 --> 00:11:05,020
The closing assembly of our second year is about to start!

163
00:11:17,550 --> 00:11:18,950
Issei...

164
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:21,020
How are things going on the mountain?

165
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:25,450
The rebuilding of the main hall just got underway.

166
00:11:26,150 --> 00:11:28,080
Everyone's working hard.

167
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:32,080
Times such as these truly test a head priest's mettle.

168
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:35,440
Admittedly, I'm barely even a novice...

169
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:39,140
But it's enough to make me want to 
bow in gratitude to our parishioners.

170
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:41,840
Yeah, I'll come by to help out soon.

171
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:44,660
That reminds me, how is Shinji doing?

172
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:47,100
He's been in the hospital for quite some time.

173
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:48,980
Oh, don't worry.

174
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:51,300
He should be discharged any day now.

175
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,610
Sakura's been going to visit him daily.

176
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:58,440
Oh, his little sister is checking in on him every day, eh?

177
00:11:58,440 --> 00:12:01,910
Yeah, from what I can see, she's worn Shinji down.

178
00:12:01,910 --> 00:12:03,360
Sakura's a tenacious girl,

179
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:05,990
so he's been browbeaten into letting her look after him.

180
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:09,000
That's wonderful news.

181
00:12:16,370 --> 00:12:18,590
Just the two kids I was looking for!

182
00:12:23,150 --> 00:12:27,040
It's been a month since anyone's heard from him,

183
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:30,600
and we have a new teacher starting next semester.

184
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:36,130
We'll look after Kuzuki-sensei's personal effects at the temple.

185
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:39,150
He turned up at the temple out of nowhere in the first place,

186
00:12:39,510 --> 00:12:41,890
so I suppose it's fitting that he left us the same way.

187
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:53,140
Well, if it isn't the student council president.

188
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:55,420
Already up and patrolling the school?

189
00:12:55,990 --> 00:12:59,420
Or are you doing maintenance on the club rooms?

190
00:13:00,210 --> 00:13:01,300
Tohsaka!

191
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:03,750
I tire of saying it so often,

192
00:13:03,750 --> 00:13:06,430
but you really are diligent that way, aren't you?

193
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:10,190
I've grown rather tired of our rote exchanges, myself!

194
00:13:10,190 --> 00:13:12,910
Why not try guessing something new every once in a while?

195
00:13:12,910 --> 00:13:16,810
I'm sure you haven't been deliberately 
repeating yourself, have you, Tohsaka?

196
00:13:16,810 --> 00:13:19,360
Of course I have.

197
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:22,050
What? You never figured that out?

198
00:13:22,050 --> 00:13:24,320
Ryuudou-kun sure is uptight,

199
00:13:25,070 --> 00:13:27,460
don't you think?

200
00:13:28,370 --> 00:13:30,740
Wh-What's the meaning of this, Emiya?!

201
00:13:31,150 --> 00:13:34,370
What manner of relationship are you in with this foul vixen?!

202
00:13:34,370 --> 00:13:35,210
Uh, I...

203
00:13:35,210 --> 00:13:38,470
Anyway, come get me in my classroom later, Emiya-kun.

204
00:13:38,470 --> 00:13:40,710
I'll wait until you get there.

205
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:42,640
Wh-What in the world?

206
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:44,220
Oh!

207
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:46,840
There you are, President!

208
00:13:47,470 --> 00:13:49,760
Mitsuzuri Ayako...

209
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:53,470
Would you mind explaining the new budget?

210
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:56,740
Why does my club's funding have to be slashed?

211
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:58,600
The archery club isn't the only one!

212
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:02,200
All club budgets have had to be reviewed.

213
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,110
I don't buy it!

214
00:14:04,110 --> 00:14:07,540
You'll stand right there and explain yourself!

215
00:14:13,450 --> 00:14:14,870
Say, Emiya-kun...

216
00:14:14,870 --> 00:14:17,260
Were you ever in the track club?

217
00:14:17,260 --> 00:14:19,010
Track club?

218
00:14:19,010 --> 00:14:22,760
No, I was always in the archery club.

219
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:24,220
Oh...

220
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:27,470
Well, I guess these things happen.

221
00:14:27,470 --> 00:14:29,890
I was just looking at the sunset, and it reminded me.

222
00:14:30,310 --> 00:14:33,520
You have to admit, it's flown by in a flash.

223
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:39,640
It's been a month since the Holy Grail War ended 
and you signed on as my pupil.

224
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:42,520
At this rate, the next year will fly by.

225
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:46,280
After that happens, we'll be leaving this school behind.

226
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:50,030
What do you plan to do after graduation?

227
00:14:50,950 --> 00:14:53,030
Follow in your father's footsteps?

228
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:56,100
Uh, yeah... Why?

229
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:59,650
After I graduate, I'm going to London.

230
00:14:59,650 --> 00:15:03,540
In light of everything that happened, 
the Mages' Association wrote me a letter of recommendation.

231
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:07,530
London? The Mages' Association's headquarters?

232
00:15:07,530 --> 00:15:09,050
That Clock Tower place?

233
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:13,330
I've been invited as the Tohsaka family heir.

234
00:15:13,330 --> 00:15:17,350
They say I can bring a pupil with me if I like.

235
00:15:18,010 --> 00:15:19,980
Um, does that mean...

236
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:22,670
So.

237
00:15:24,140 --> 00:15:25,790
What will you be doing?

238
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:32,080
Damn it. You always go right for my weak spot.

239
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:33,790
What?

240
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:35,740
Look...

241
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:39,700
This is important, so give me a straight answer.

242
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:42,500
Will you come with me?

243
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:48,760
Don't ask when you already know the answer.

244
00:15:50,030 --> 00:15:53,010
Then let's keep up the good work, Emiya-kun!

245
00:15:54,010 --> 00:15:59,680
I'm gonna whip you into shape until 
you're a proper mage, so brace yourself!

246
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:06,080
My life's goal is to make you into a new man—
one who's happy through and through.

247
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:19,790
Thanks for bringing me with you.

248
00:16:57,180 --> 00:16:57,990
Excuse me.

249
00:16:58,610 --> 00:17:01,760
You are the exchange student from Japan?

250
00:17:02,790 --> 00:17:04,870
Actually, that would be Tohsaka.

251
00:17:04,870 --> 00:17:07,270
I know that.

252
00:17:07,270 --> 00:17:10,210
I was referring to you.

253
00:17:10,210 --> 00:17:12,510
You're from Fuyuki City in Japan, right?

254
00:17:13,150 --> 00:17:15,860
You don't seem to have the makings of a mage.

255
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:22,270
I imagine you were an outsider who was caught up in the ritual and missed his chance to get out?

256
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:24,610
I find it puzzling.

257
00:17:24,610 --> 00:17:27,830
After surviving that troublesome war,

258
00:17:27,830 --> 00:17:30,910
to what end have you come to Clock Tower?

259
00:17:30,910 --> 00:17:33,280
To what end do you study magic?

260
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,110
Good question.

261
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:39,460
Since coming here, I've learned many things,

262
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:42,040
and in many ways, I've been out of my depth.

263
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:46,130
But I want to keep believing in what I believed in before.

264
00:17:46,130 --> 00:17:49,570
I want to dedicate my life to that.

265
00:17:49,570 --> 00:17:51,300
Meaning what, exactly?

266
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:55,300
Well, I realize how dumb this sounds...

267
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:58,140
But I want to become something.

268
00:18:00,140 --> 00:18:02,310
A champion of justice.

269
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:09,570
I see. That certainly is idiotic.

270
00:18:09,570 --> 00:18:11,250
But it is nothing to laugh at.

271
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,840
A champion of justice, hmm?

272
00:18:14,690 --> 00:18:18,130
Yes, I suppose such a man would find this place stifling.

273
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,530
Tohsaka?

274
00:18:28,530 --> 00:18:30,960
Did we have plans for dinner?

275
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:34,460
I was waiting for you.

276
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,720
Well? What did you do about enrollment?

277
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:41,970
Oh, I turned them down.

278
00:18:43,970 --> 00:18:46,230
You're not angry?

279
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:49,660
I knew this would happen.

280
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:53,720
Oh, but if you aren't going to join Clock Tower,

281
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:56,990
I guess that means I'll be thrown out in three years too.

282
00:18:57,290 --> 00:18:59,740
No, that doesn't mean you have to—

283
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:04,740
Are you sure, though?

284
00:19:04,740 --> 00:19:07,370
I've been thinking about it nonstop,

285
00:19:07,370 --> 00:19:10,780
but I don't think I'll ever be able to change how I live.

286
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:15,500
Even when I know I'm not right, I can't change paths.

287
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,560
It's just as he said...

288
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:22,740
I'll meet the same fate.

289
00:19:22,740 --> 00:19:25,440
He's right. I agree with him there.

290
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:27,640
You're full of mistakes, Shirou.

291
00:19:27,970 --> 00:19:32,280
You're probably on the same path, 
heading in the same direction.

292
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:35,900
The difference might be in how far you can go.

293
00:19:36,630 --> 00:19:42,140
What matters is where you end up, 
and how far you came, right?

294
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:45,410
Even if your destination 
and the result end up being the same,

295
00:19:45,410 --> 00:19:48,470
if you manage to walk a little further afterward,

296
00:19:48,470 --> 00:19:51,620
I know you'll get your proper ending.

297
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:53,790
I see.

298
00:19:53,790 --> 00:19:56,130
I really hope it turns out like that.

299
00:19:56,130 --> 00:20:00,330
No, I guess hoping isn't enough. 
I need to make sure that's what happens.

300
00:20:00,330 --> 00:20:01,880
I wouldn't worry.

301
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:05,640
I mean, you've had your answer all along.

302
00:20:06,060 --> 00:20:07,520
But are you really sure?

303
00:20:07,950 --> 00:20:11,860
Clock Tower is an important place to you, right?

304
00:20:11,860 --> 00:20:13,520
I'll be fine.

305
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:16,150
In the end, I'll probably settle down at Clock Tower.

306
00:20:16,150 --> 00:20:19,420
But I want to look around and get things out of my system.

307
00:20:19,420 --> 00:20:21,530
You know, see the world.

308
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:25,160
So now it's my turn to drag you around with me, huh?

309
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:28,630
Yeah, though that's all a ways off yet.

310
00:20:30,190 --> 00:20:35,420
Regardless, having fun, suffering, seeing the sights,

311
00:20:35,790 --> 00:20:38,800
and eventually having our own happily ever after...

312
00:20:41,520 --> 00:20:44,340
That's the future in store for us.

313
00:22:41,280 --> 00:22:42,860
A boy once said,

314
00:22:43,800 --> 00:22:45,920
"I don't want to watch people die."

315
00:22:46,730 --> 00:22:52,180
"Shouldn't it be possible to save all who suffer?"

316
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:56,940
What the boy was trying to cut down was himself.

317
00:22:57,920 --> 00:23:00,870
He wielded his sword for what he came to believe in.

318
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:06,690
There is no longer a path where his battle ends and he turns back.

319
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:11,040
However, he did get his answer.

320
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:12,560
He has regrets.

321
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:15,450
And he doesn't know how many times 
he has wished to do it all over.

322
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,900
This fate is set in stone,

323
00:23:18,900 --> 00:23:21,080
and Emiya will probably go on cursing it.

324
00:23:22,190 --> 00:23:23,210
But even still,

325
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:27,670
I was not wrong.

